 "nl": [
  "iot-sensors may use any UDP port towards guest-wifi, except SNMP (UDP 161), TFTP (UDP 69), which must be blocked.",
  "Permit TCP ports 1024-65535 from ops to dns-servers but deny RDP (TCP 3389), PostgreSQL (TCP 5432), MySQL (TCP 3306).",
  "engineering offers DNS over UDP 53 and HTTPS (TCP 443) to every zone.",
  "edge-cache must never reach engineering, regardless of any other rule.",
  "Make HTTP (TCP 80) and HTTPS (TCP 443) on dns-servers reachable from all internal zones.",
  "Restrict vpn-users so that its only permitted destinations are nvr on HTTPS (TCP 443); drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "guest-wifi must accept SMTP (TCP 25) and RTSP (TCP 554) and syslog (UDP 514) from vpn-users.",
  "Deny all traffic from nvr to mail (this overrides any public service).",
  "dns-servers is isolated: it may only reach guest-wifi on syslog (UDP 514), and nothing else.",
  "Permit any UDP port from dns-servers to iot-sensors but deny SNMP (UDP 161), TFTP (UDP 69).",
  "Allow nvr to connect to engineering using NTP (UDP 123) and HTTPS (TCP 443) and SMB (TCP 445).",
  "Hosts in vpn-users may reach mail over HTTP (TCP 80) and RTSP (TCP 554).",
  "Allow nvr to connect to iot-sensors using SMTP (TCP 25).",
  "mail must accept DNS over UDP 53 and RTSP (TCP 554) and HTTPS (TCP 443) from dev-lab.",
  "Permit TCP ports 1024-65535 from dev-lab to dns-servers but deny MySQL (TCP 3306), RDP (TCP 3389)."
 ],
